1
00:00:00,310 --> 00:00:01,200
One of the most common

2
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,400
questions we get is,

3
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:03,490
how do I know if

4
00:00:03,490 --> 00:00:04,890
I'm actually a candidate for

5
00:00:04,890 --> 00:00:05,990
spinal decompression?

6
00:00:05,990 --> 00:00:07,590
And the answer really depends

7
00:00:07,590 --> 00:00:08,900
on what's causing your problem.

8
00:00:09,380 --> 00:00:11,300
We commonly evaluate decompression as

9
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:12,510
an option for people dealing

10
00:00:12,510 --> 00:00:13,980
with chronic lower back pain,

11
00:00:14,230 --> 00:00:15,470
certain disc problems,

12
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:16,870
degenerative changes,

13
00:00:16,870 --> 00:00:18,080
or pain that may travel

14
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:19,400
into the hip or leg,

15
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:20,820
what many people simply call

16
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:21,430
sciatica.

17
00:00:21,910 --> 00:00:23,110
A typical patient might tell

18
00:00:23,110 --> 00:00:23,360
me,

19
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:24,410
I can stand for a

20
00:00:24,410 --> 00:00:24,990
little while,

21
00:00:24,990 --> 00:00:26,120
but then my back starts

22
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:26,520
hurting,

23
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:27,980
or I get pain,

24
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:28,510
numbness,

25
00:00:28,510 --> 00:00:29,660
or tingling going down my

26
00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:30,360
leg.

27
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:31,150
Those are the kinds of

28
00:00:31,150 --> 00:00:32,630
symptoms we want to investigate.

29
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:34,110
But here's what's important.

30
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:35,750
Not everyone with back pain

31
00:00:35,750 --> 00:00:36,730
needs decompression.

32
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:38,520
Sometimes the problem is coming

33
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:39,680
primarily from a joint,

34
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:40,530
a muscle,

35
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:41,320
the hip,

36
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:42,640
or something else entirely.

37
00:00:43,090 --> 00:00:44,210
And there are certain medical

38
00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:46,270
conditions where decompression may not

39
00:00:46,270 --> 00:00:46,970
be appropriate.

40
00:00:47,350 --> 00:00:48,520
That's why we don't simply

41
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:49,910
put everyone who walks through

42
00:00:49,910 --> 00:00:50,920
the door on the machine.

43
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:52,580
We start by listening to

44
00:00:52,580 --> 00:00:53,380
what's happening,

45
00:00:53,590 --> 00:00:54,530
examining you,

46
00:00:54,740 --> 00:00:56,280
and reviewing any X-rays or

47
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:57,770
MRI studies when appropriate.

48
00:00:58,220 --> 00:00:59,760
Then we determine what treatment

49
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:01,350
or combination of treatments makes

50
00:01:01,350 --> 00:01:02,150
the most sense.

51
00:01:02,590 --> 00:01:03,530
So if you're wondering whether

52
00:01:03,530 --> 00:01:04,410
you're a candidate,

53
00:01:04,660 --> 00:01:05,360
you don't have to figure

54
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:06,180
that out yourself.

55
00:01:06,350 --> 00:01:07,130
That's our job.

56
00:01:07,480 --> 00:01:08,280
Give us a call,

57
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:09,600
and we'll help you determine

58
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:11,650
whether spinal decompression makes sense

59
00:01:11,650 --> 00:01:13,060
for your particular condition.
